  "catalogReviewNotes": [
    "2026-09-07: K Mathematics review authored against the 206-primitive live export (K Language Arts pilot + letter-workshop, you-and-me, story-bridge, di-deduction, di-worked-procedure). Legacy target_primitive/target_eval_modes on the published rows are provenance only; 22 of them point at knowledge-check and 3 at balance-scale for weight, which this review does not inherit.",
    "2026-09-07 (same day, later): literacy.ts gained the story-bridge entry (K Language Arts, match_character) while this review was being authored. It has no K Mathematics home and touches no math/di/calendar/assessment/core entry, so all 166 decisions stand. The basis is now scoped to the six catalog files this review's edges can cite; the review asserts that scoping.",
    "2026-09-08: ten-frame gained build_teen (beta 2.0) and decompose_teen (beta 3.0), number-bond gained ten_and_ones (beta 2.0) — the K.NBT.1 fork recorded in docs/contracts/ten-frame.md R2. The seven K.NBT.1 rows (COUNT001-05-A..F, COUNT001-03-G) were re-reviewed against the new modes before this refresh; no other row's capabilities changed.",
    "Slice 5 (reader-fit re-audit of the Grade-1 band floors, 2026-09-08). math.ts: ten floors lowered to Kindergarten across sorting-station (sort_attribute, sort_variety, count_compare, two_attributes, tally_record), compare-objects (order_three), length-lab (order) and time-sequencer (sequence-5, before-after, duration-compare); read-schedule and number-bond fact_family HELD as WRONG-BAND at PRE. Every edit cites qa/reader-fit/k-band-floor-2026-09-08.md. Seventeen decisions re-reviewed: 13 partial to candidate, 3 partial with a new home, PTRN001-03-C re-probed clean after the time-sequencer P1 fix.",
    "2026-09-09: catalog re-exported (208 primitives) after slices 2-7. Reviewed changes against the frozen decisions: bar-model +read_one_to_one/most_least/match_to_bar/build_one_to_one (K data, slice 7); counting-board +give_me_n/recount_moved/add_more/take_away (slice 7); analog-clock +hand_name/count_face/hear_time (slice 7); measure-lab NEW (balance_predict/capacity_predict/pour_count/order_capacity, slice 7); constraint or mode-text refreshes on pattern-builder, hundreds-chart, number-bond, sorting-station, length-lab, time-sequencer, compare-objects (slices 4-6). No existing reviewed edge lost its mode. New modes are re-pointed by the slice that ships them; until then their rows keep the prior verdict. Provenance for draws now hashes each primitive's own catalog entry rather than the catalog file.",
    "2026-09-09 (later): catalog re-exported; changes since the previous note: CHANGED length-lab +estimate_then_tile,two_unit_compare description/constraints;. Slice-7 additions; no cited edge lost its mode; new modes are re-pointed by their slice.",
    "2026-09-09 (slice-7 re-point): edges re-pointed to bar-model K data modes, counting-board give_me_n/recount_moved/add_more/take_away/count_on(K), measure-lab (new), analog-clock hand_name/count_face/hear_time, length-lab estimate_then_tile/two_unit_compare + body-part units, per the slice-7 session's live probes and Chrome drives. Catalog changes since the previous note: no catalog changes since the export;",
    "2026-09-09 (rebuild): catalog changes since the previous note: CHANGED shape-sorter description;. No cited edge lost its mode.",
    "2026-09-09 (slice 3 close, strategy-picker objective window): math.ts strategy-picker constraints re-worded from \"Numbers within 5 (K) or 10 (Grade 1)\" to name the band as the DEFAULT and the objective as the scope, with a stated ceiling of 10. The only capability change is that strategy-picker is now placeable on a K requirement that names a range up to 10; no eval mode, description or other entry changed. The rows this widens (OPS001-01-E/F, OPS001-02-E) were re-probed live the same day at maxNumber 10 with sums 6-10 — qa/eval-reports/objective-window-caps-2026-09-09.json — so the affected decisions were reviewed before this hash refresh, not silenced by it.",
    "Slice 7 (2026-09-09), the two HELD band floors from the 09-08 re-audit. math.ts: number-bond gains related_fact (beta 3.0, K+G1) -- the SPOKEN fact family, one bond and two judged turns, built because a K probe of the missing_part redirect returned ten unknown-addend turns with no subtraction anywhere; time-sequencer gains clock-sequence (beta 3.5, K) -- ordering activity cards that each carry an analog clock FACE at a whole hour, built because analog-clock read has no sequence and sequence-5 bans clock times at K, so the two halves of TIME001-03-G could never meet. fact_family and read-schedule KEEP their Grade-1 floors and their prose now names the K redirect. Three rows re-pointed partial -> candidate: OPS001-02-G, OPS001-03-F, TIME001-03-G. Also frozen but NOT this slice's change: strategy-picker constraints, another session's objective-window widening (K default 5, raised to 10 when the objective names it) -- inspected here only far enough to confirm it widens rather than narrows and touches none of these three rows."
